Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/assets/7bd0200a651aec7283e5c96d3cdc1589d795531e179ca0eb7cc36ef5bad8de56.png)\n\nWe're given that the velocity function $v(x)$ is\n\n$$\nv(x)=4-2x.\n$$\n\nWe know that $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ Therefore, we have the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=4-2x.\n$$\n\nSeparating the variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =4-2x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4-2x}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{4-2x}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{4-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x| & =t+K \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x| & =-2t-2K \\\\ 2-x & =C{e}^{-2t} \\\\ x & =2-C{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=0$ when $t=0.$ Therefore, $C=2,$ and the particular solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)=2-2{e}^{-2t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7aab2d70df29993bcf3933ea0964c05d6c71bd11eb5e3841881fcf936561eec"} {"question" "q-122321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "785f7610edd208db81cfb7c4ec13a140b5ce47e04ba0e053de3c67f7552cdd94"} {"question" "q-122321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "c7aab2d70df29993bcf3933ea0964c05d6c71bd11eb5e3841881fcf936561eec"} {"question" "q-122321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["ma